+# Pakpost v27 — Browser Extension Interceptor
+
+- Settings → Interceptor: Secure Proxy (default), Browser (CORS), Browser Extension (Chrome/Edge/Firefox).
+- The extension popup manages **Allowed Pakpost Origins** and **Allowed API Destinations** dynamically. No per-domain code rebuild.
+- `extension/dist/chrome/` and `extension/dist/firefox/` contain standalone unpacked addon builds.
+- `extension/build.sh` rebuilds both packages with **no npm/Bun dependency**.
+- Request execution keeps the existing QuickJS pre/post scripting flow and response shape.
+- Extension failures NEVER fall back to the backend proxy.
+- No backend, database, migrations, auth, Vite, Bun or QuickJS dependency changes.
+- Internal destinations work only if the user's browser has the correct LAN/VPN/DNS and browser permissions.
+- The new interceptor preference is stored in the browser under `pakpost_interceptor_mode`.
+
+See `extension/README.md` for installation and permission details.
